                <pb facs="0645" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/293a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-28T19:00:00-05:00">November 28,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>251. Is there any method by which money may be sent from the United States to
                    persons in Soviet-occupied Poland? Reply (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) with
                    regard to American citizens, and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Soviet
                    citizens.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
